# The Gradle wrapper is COMMITTED, so the four ignore rules Flutter's template
# ships for it are deliberately absent here.
#
# The wrapper is the only way `./gradlew` exists on a machine that has not run
# Flutter's Android tooling — and CI is exactly that machine. The `android-native`
# job ran `./gradlew` against a fresh checkout and got "No such file or directory"
# every single time, so the Kotlin suite that covers the mask/cutout encoders has
# never actually run. Gradle's own guidance is to check the wrapper in; this file
# was the reason we could not.
#
# `gradle-wrapper.jar` is a binary, which is the fair objection. It is pinned by
# checksum in CI: the `android-native` job validates it against Gradle's published
# list on every run, so a swapped jar fails the build rather than executing.

/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# Kotlin compiler session artifacts
.kotlin/
